mach/machine dispatch headers: accept the compiler spelling of arm64 (aarch64 port, task A4)

The machine/ dispatch headers test __arm64__, which Apple's compilers define but a HOST
aarch64-linux clang does not: it says __aarch64__. Host tools that include mach headers
(migcom is the first, via mig strdefs.h -> mach/boolean.h) then land on #error
"architecture not supported". Same one-line fix darling PR 1753 carries for boolean.h;
guest compiles (-target arm64-apple-darwin20) define both spellings and never notice.

--- a/osfmk/mach/machine/boolean.h
+++ b/osfmk/mach/machine/boolean.h
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@

 #if defined (__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
 #include "mach/i386/boolean.h"
-#elif defined (__arm__) || defined (__arm64__)
+#elif defined (__arm__) || defined (__arm64__) || defined (__aarch64__)
 #include "mach/arm/boolean.h"
 #else
 #error architecture not supported
